        "id": 10405,
        "name": "Krayden006",
        "username": "Krayden006",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/krayden006/{size}/2414_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-30T15:59:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm having trouble reconciling the Gain Credits Event text with the Example sidebar on page 8. &nbsp;The rules text says \"If additional cards are added to or removed from a player's hand after the start of the Requisition phase, that player's available credits for the phase do not change.\"</p><p>The example says \"At the beginning of the Requisition phase, a player has four cards in hand with a total Value of 100. &nbsp;They then play Even the Odds, allowing them to draw two cards. &nbsp;These two new cards have a combined Value of 50, but Even the Odds, with a Value of 20, is recycled when played. &nbsp;Consequently, the player gains 130 during the Gain Credits Event.\"</p><p>They seem to contradict each other. &nbsp;You start the phase with 100 credits. &nbsp;No matter if you add or remove cards from your hand, you have 100 credits. &nbsp;One card is played adding two cards to your hand for a net gain of 30 credits. &nbsp;Am I missing something?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:41:26.858Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 2,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 10.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 10405,
        "topic_slug": "requisition-phase-in-the-rulebook",
        "display_username": "Krayden006",
        "primary_group_name": null,
