        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I&#39;m having trouble reconciling the Gain Credits Event text with the Example sidebar on page 8. &nbsp;The rules text says &quot;If additional cards are added to or removed from a player&#39;s hand after the start of the Requisition phase, that player&#39;s available credits for the phase do not change.&quot;</p><p>The example says &quot;At the beginning of the Requisition phase, a player has four cards in hand with a total Value of 100. &nbsp;They then play Even the Odds, allowing them to draw two cards. &nbsp;These two new cards have a combined Value of 50, but Even the Odds, with a Value of 20, is recycled when played. &nbsp;Consequently, the player gains 130 during the Gain Credits Event.&quot;</p><p>They seem to contradict each other. &nbsp;You start the phase with 100 credits. &nbsp;No matter if you add or remove cards from your hand, you have 100 credits. &nbsp;One card is played adding two cards to your hand for a net gain of 30 credits. &nbsp;Am I missing something?</p>",
